---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Sol Fabricator — the open-source software factory for backend services" description="Sol Fabricator is the open-source software factory for backend services. Write OCaml or TypeScript; the sol CLI scaffolds, builds, packages, deploys, observes, and rolls back against one language-neutral contract. Apache-2.0, pre-alpha.">
  <main>
    <section class="hero shell">
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Sol home">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 42 42" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="21" cy="17" r="8"/><path d="M8 29c4-5 8-7 13-7s9 2 13 7"/><path d="M12 34h18"/></svg>
          <span>sol</span>
        </a>
        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="#how">How it works</a>
          <a href="#platform">Architecture</a>
          <a href="#principles">Principles</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/blob/main/docs/guides/TUTORIAL.md">Docs</a>
        </div>
        <a class="nav-cta" href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>

      <div class="hero-main">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Open-source software factory</p>
          <h1>Build.<br/>Deploy.<br/><em>Own it.</em></h1>
          <p class="lede">Write OCaml or TypeScript. Sol scaffolds, builds, packages, deploys, observes, and rolls back backend services against one language-neutral contract.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="#install">Get started <span>→</span></a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/blob/main/docs/guides/TUTORIAL.md">Read the tutorial</a>
          </div>
          <p class="status-strip"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Pre-alpha · v0.1.0-alpha · not production-stable<a href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/blob/main/docs/planning/ROADMAP.md">Roadmap ↗</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-note" aria-hidden="true">Local by default.<br/>Yours in production.<span>↙</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-features" aria-label="What Sol gives you">
        <article><b>⌘</b><div><h2>Open source</h2><p>Apache-2.0. Your Kubernetes cluster, your cloud account, your data.</p></div></article>
        <article><b>✦</b><div><h2>OCaml or TypeScript</h2><p>Two first-class application languages behind one operational contract.</p></div></article>
        <article><b>⚡</b><div><h2>Local mirrors prod</h2><p>k3d locally with the same Helm charts, service DNS, and security model.</p></div></article>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-terminal" id="install">
        <div class="hero-terminal-tabs"><span class="active">Terminal</span><span>Deploy</span><span>Status</span><span>Logs</span><span>Rollback</span><button class="copy" aria-label="Copy quickstart commands" data-copy={"sol local infra up\nsol new workspace myapp\ncd myapp && sol up"}>Copy</button></div>
        <div class="hero-terminal-body">
          <pre><span class="prompt">$</span> sol local infra up
<span class="prompt">$</span> sol new workspace myapp
<span class="prompt">$</span> cd myapp && sol up

<span class="success">✓ k3d cluster: redpanda · postgres · loki · grafana</span>
<span class="success">✓ charge_svc deployed · worker consuming events</span>
<span class="success">✓ curl localhost:8080/health → ok</span></pre>
          <p aria-hidden="true">Local by default.<br/>Yours in production.<span>↙</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="platform-panel shell" id="platform">
      <div class="platform-intro">
        <p class="section-label">The platform</p>
        <h2>One contract.<br/>Every primitive.</h2>
        <p class="platform-lede">Sol compiles a workspace of services, workers, and scheduled functions into typed deployment plans, then runs them on Kubernetes — locally or in your own cloud account. You write domain logic; Sol owns the lifecycle.</p>
        <div class="cloud-choice"><span>Run on</span><b>AWS</b><i>or</i><b>Google Cloud</b><i>or</i><b>any Kubernetes</b><small>AWS and GCP provisioning are experimental; any conformant cluster works.</small></div>
        <div class="platform-benefits">
          <article><span>ϟ</span><div><h3>Three primitives</h3><p><code>_svc</code> HTTP services, <code>_worker</code> Kafka consumers, <code>_fn</code> scheduled jobs.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>◇</span><div><h3>Typed events</h3><p>Domains integrate through schema-registry events, never shared code.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>♢</span><div><h3>Dev mirrors prod</h3><p>The same Helm charts, service DNS, and security model locally on k3d.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>⌘</span><div><h3>Observability wired in</h3><p>Structured logs, metrics, and traces from the first message — no instrumentation.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="platform-stack" aria-label="Sol platform layers">
        <div class="stack-spine"></div>
        <article class="stack-card stack-app"><span>⌁</span><b>Your App</b></article>
        <article class="stack-card stack-sol"><span>◉</span><b>Sol Factory</b></article>
        <article class="stack-card stack-infra"><span>⬡</span><b>Kubernetes</b></article>
        <article class="stack-card stack-world"><span>⌁</span><b>Your Cloud Account</b></article>
        <p class="stack-note">From code<br/>to production.<span>↖</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deploy-model shell" aria-labelledby="deploy-model-title">
      <div class="deploy-model-head">
        <div><p class="section-label">One contract, end to end</p><h2 id="deploy-model-title">You bring the code.<br/><span>Sol runs the system.</span></h2></div>
        <p>Choose the primitive that matches the work. Sol discovers it, verifies the runtime contract, builds an immutable artifact, and operates it on the destination you selected.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="primitive-row" aria-label="Sol application primitives">
        <article><code>_svc</code><div><h3>Service</h3><p>Long-running HTTP applications and APIs.</p></div></article>
        <article><code>_worker</code><div><h3>Worker</h3><p>Background consumers and continuous processing.</p></div></article>
        <article><code>_fn</code><div><h3>Function</h3><p>Finite jobs and event-driven execution.</p></div></article>
      </div>
      <div class="deploy-flow" aria-label="How Sol deploys an application">
        <article><span>01</span><b>Your repository</b><small>Dockerfile + unit convention</small></article>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <article><span>02</span><b>Contract check</b><small>port · health · metrics · shutdown</small></article>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <article><span>03</span><b>Build &amp; release</b><small>digest-pinned, recorded, reversible</small></article>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <article><span>04</span><b>Operate</b><small>logs · traces · metrics · rollback</small></article>
      </div>
      <div class="contract-card">
        <div><span>Runtime contract</span><code>PORT</code><code>GET /healthz</code><code>GET /metrics</code><code>SIGTERM drain</code></div>
        <p><b>Sol handles the rest.</b> Infrastructure integration, observability, rollout state, and operational evidence travel with every release.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="playground shell" id="how">
      <div class="playground-head">
        <div><p class="section-label">Deployment preview</p><h2>One CLI.<br/><span>One contract.</span></h2><p>The same workflow carries every primitive from source to a healthy, observable release — on k3d or your own Kubernetes cluster.</p></div>
        <p class="preview-caption">A representative Sol run</p>
      </div>
      <div class="playground-grid">
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true">1<br/>2<br/>3<br/>4<br/>5<br/>6<br/>7</div>
          <pre><span class="prompt">$</span> sol new workspace myapp
<span class="prompt">$</span> cd myapp
<span class="prompt">$</span> sol up

→ Discovering app/*/*_svc · _worker · _fn
→ Building images · rendering manifests
<span class="success">✓ Deployed · curl localhost:8080/health → ok</span></pre>
          <button class="copy demo-copy" aria-label="Copy playground commands" data-copy={"sol new workspace myapp\ncd myapp\nsol up"}>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="play-actions" aria-label="Deployment capabilities">
          <article class="selected"><span>⬡</span><div><b>Deploy a service</b><small>Build, release, and verify health</small></div></article>
          <article><span>◇</span><div><b>Connect data</b><small>PostgreSQL with typed access and migrations</small></div></article>
          <article><span>▣</span><div><b>Configure the environment</b><small>Settings and secrets per environment</small></div></article>
          <article><span>⌁</span><div><b>Operate with evidence</b><small>Release inspection, logs, and rollback</small></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="playground-cta"><div><h3>Ready to build something real?</h3><p>Start on your machine, ship to your own Kubernetes.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/releases">Download the alpha <span>→</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="principles shell" id="principles">
      <div class="principles-head">
        <p class="section-label">03 / Design principles</p>
        <h2>Strong defaults.<br/><em>Clear escape hatches.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-list">
        <article><span>Ⅰ</span><div><h3>Language neutral</h3><p>If it speaks HTTP, exposes health and metrics, and shuts down cleanly, Sol can run it.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Ⅱ</span><div><h3>CLI first</h3><p>The full operational path is scriptable, composable, and legible without a proprietary control panel.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Ⅲ</span><div><h3>Evidence over magic</h3><p>Builds, releases, and destinations stay inspectable. When something fails, the evidence survives.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Ⅳ</span><div><h3>Local is a real mode</h3><p>The local path is explicit and safe, with the same application contract and no chance of resolving to production.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing shell">
      <div class="closing-sun"></div>
      <p class="section-label">Start with one service</p>
      <h2>Make production<br/><em>boring again.</em></h2>
      <p>Start on k3d locally. Ship to your own Kubernetes cluster when you're ready.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol">Star on GitHub <span>→</span></a><a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/blob/main/docs/guides/TUTORIAL.md">Read the tutorial</a></div>
    </section>

    <footer class="shell">
      <div class="footer-brand">
        <a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 42 42" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="21" cy="17" r="8"/><path d="M8 29c4-5 8-7 13-7s9 2 13 7"/><path d="M12 34h18"/></svg><span>sol</span></a>
        <p>Sol Fabricator — open-source software factory for backend services. Apache-2.0.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-right">
        <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Project links">
          <a href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/blob/main/docs/guides/TUTORIAL.md">Tutorial</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/releases">Releases</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/loganbnielsen/sol/blob/main/docs/planning/ROADMAP.md">Roadmap</a>
        </nav>
        <span>© 2026 Sol Fabricator · Apache-2.0</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy ?? '');
        button.textContent = 'Copied';
        window.setTimeout(() => button.textContent = 'Copy', 1400);
      });
    });
  </script>
</Base>
